-- title:
--   A value attained too often lies in the base field
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ an $F$-algebra, let $g \in F[Y]$ be a polynomial with coefficients in $F$, let $x \in L$, and let $s$ be a finite subset of $L$. Assume that the natural degree of $g$ is strictly smaller than the cardinality of $s$, and that for every $y \in s$ the value of $g$ at $y$ under the $F$-algebra evaluation map $L[Y] \to L$ induced by $y$ (that is, $g$ evaluated at $y$ after pushing its coefficients into $L$ along the structure map) equals $x$. The conclusion is that $x$ lies in the range of the algebra map $F \to L$, i.e. $x$ is the image of an element of $F$. Note that the hypothesis uses `natDegree`, so the degenerate case $g = 0$ is covered: there the hypothesis merely requires $s$ to be nonempty, and the value $x$ is then $0$, which is indeed in the range.
--
--   This is the elementary statement that a polynomial over $F$ of degree less than $\#s$ which is constant on $s$ has its constant value in $F$ — equivalently, that the nonzero polynomial $g - x$ could not have $\#s$ roots in $L$ unless $x$ comes from $F$. It is used in the analysis of the function field of the modular curve $X_0(N)$, in the proof that the relevant $j$-value does not lie in the subalgebra generated by the modular polynomial's other root.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Polynomial_mem_range_of_eval_eq_const.lean

import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Splits

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem Polynomial.mem_range_of_eval_eq_const {F L : Type*} [Field F] [Field L] [Algebra F L] (g : Polynomial F) (x : L) (s : Finset L) (hcard : g.natDegree < s.card) (hval : ∀ y ∈ s, Polynomial.aeval y g = x) : x ∈ (algebraMap F L).range := by sorry
